OVERVIEW: Send DICOM images to printer

Sends DICOM images to a DICOM printer using the Print Management Service.
Supports single images, multiple images with automatic layout, and templates.

Examples:
  # Print single image
  dicom-print send pacs://server:11112 image.dcm --aet WORKSTATION

  # Print with custom options
  dicom-print send pacs://server:11112 scan.dcm --aet APP \
      --copies 2 --film-size 14x17 --orientation landscape

  # Print multiple images with layout
  dicom-print send pacs://server:11112 *.dcm --aet APP --layout 2x3

  # A scout over its slices: one image in the top row, three beneath
  dicom-print send pacs://server:11112 *.dcm --aet APP --layout 'ROW\1,3'

  # Print directory recursively
  dicom-print send pacs://server:11112 studies/ --aet APP --recursive

USAGE: dicom-print send [<options>] <url> <paths> ... --aet <aet>

ARGUMENTS:
  <url>                   Printer URL (pacs://host:port)
  <paths>                 DICOM files or directories to print

OPTIONS:
  --aet <aet>             Local Application Entity Title (calling AE)
  --called-aet <called-aet>
                          Remote Application Entity Title (default: ANY-SCP)
                          (default: ANY-SCP)
  --copies <copies>       Number of Copies (2000,0010), 1 or more (default: 1)
                          (default: 1)
  --film-size <film-size> Film Size ID (2010,0050), PS3.3 Table C.13-3; token
                          (Defined Term, also accepted): 8x10 = 8INX10IN,
                          8.5x11 = 8_5INX11IN, 10x12 = 10INX12IN, 10x14 =
                          10INX14IN, 11x14 = 11INX14IN, 11x17 = 11INX17IN,
                          14x14 = 14INX14IN, 14x17 = 14INX17IN, 24x24cm =
                          24CMX24CM, 24x30cm = 24CMX30CM, a4 = A4, a3 = A3
                          (default: 14x17) (default: 14x17)
  --orientation <orientation>
                          Film Orientation (2010,0040): portrait = PORTRAIT,
                          landscape = LANDSCAPE (default: portrait) (default:
                          portrait)
  --priority <priority>   Print Priority (2000,0020), PS3.3 Table C.13-1: low =
                          LOW, medium = MED, high = HIGH (default: medium)
                          (default: medium)
  --layout <layout>       Image Display Format (2010,0010): a grid RxC (1x1 to
                          4x5; R rows by C columns, sent as STANDARD\C,R) or
                          any PS3.3 Table C.13-3 form — STANDARD\C,R,
                          ROW\R1,R2,..., COL\C1,C2,..., SLIDE, SUPERSLIDE,
                          CUSTOM\i (quote it, the shell eats backslashes); auto
                          if not specified (values: 1x1, 1x2, 1x3, 1x4, 2x1,
                          2x2, 2x3, 2x4, 3x1, 3x2, 3x3, 3x4, 4x1, 4x2, 4x3,
                          4x4, 4x5, ROW\1,2, ROW\2,3, COL\1,2, COL\1,3,
                          COL\1,4, COL\1,4,4, COL\2,4,4)
  --template <template>   Layout preset: single, comparison, grid, multi-phase
                          (sets layout + film size + orientation; conflicts
                          with --layout)
  --medium <medium>       Medium Type (2000,0030), PS3.3 Table C.13-1: paper =
                          PAPER, clear-film = CLEAR FILM, blue-film = BLUE
                          FILM, mammo-clear-film = MAMMO CLEAR FILM,
                          mammo-blue-film = MAMMO BLUE FILM (default: paper)
                          (default: paper)
  --magnification <magnification>
                          Magnification Type (2010,0060): replicate =
                          REPLICATE, bilinear = BILINEAR, cubic = CUBIC, none =
                          NONE (default: replicate) (default: replicate)
  --film-destination <film-destination>
                          Film Destination (2000,0040): magazine = MAGAZINE,
                          processor = PROCESSOR, bin-1 = BIN_1, bin-2 = BIN_2,
                          ... bin-N = BIN_N (default: processor). PS3.3 Table
                          C.13-1 numbers sorter bins from 1 with no maximum;
                          any bin-N / BIN_N is sent (no leading zeros)
                          (default: processor)
  --check-status          N-GET Printer Status (2110,0010) before printing;
                          abort on FAILURE, warn on WARNING
  --verify                Perform a C-ECHO connectivity check against the
                          printer before printing
  --format <format>       Output format: text, json (json writes the result
                          object to stdout; diagnostics stay on stderr)
                          (default: text)
  --color <color>         Meta SOP Class negotiated: grayscale = Basic
                          Grayscale Print Management Meta SOP Class
                          (1.2.840.10008.5.1.1.9), color = Basic Color Print
                          Management Meta SOP Class (1.2.840.10008.5.1.1.18)
                          (default: grayscale) (default: grayscale)
  --frame <frame>         1-based frame to print from multi-frame files
                          (default: 1) (default: 1)
  --all-frames            Print every frame of multi-frame files (one image box
                          per frame)
  --raw                   Send stored pixel values without preprocessing (no
                          rescale/window/inversion). Compressed sources are
                          still decoded.
  --window-center <window-center>
                          Explicit VOI window center (requires --window-width;
                          overrides the data set's window)
  --window-width <window-width>
                          Explicit VOI window width (requires --window-center)
  --bit-depth <bit-depth> Grayscale output bit depth: 8 or 12 (default: 8).
                          PS3.3 Table C.13-5 allows Bits Stored of 8 or 12
                          only; 12 sends 12-in-16 P-Values. A higher value is
                          clamped, not refused. (default: 8)
  --presentation-lut <presentation-lut>
                          Presentation LUT Shape (2050,0020), PS3.3 Table
                          C.11-4: identity = IDENTITY, inverse, lin-od = LIN OD
                          (default: none, no Presentation LUT is created)
  --palette <palette>     Pseudo-colour palette baked into the pixels (default:
                          none, grayscale).
        Grayscale: grayscale, grayscale-inverse
        DICOM Standard: hot-iron, pet, hot-metal-blue, pet-20-step, spring,
        summer, fall, winter
        Perceptually Uniform: viridis, inferno, magma, plasma
        Spectrum: jet, rainbow, gray-rainbow, spectrum
        Single Hue & Flow: hot-green, hue-1, hue-2, flow, ratio

        Colour is baked into 8-bit RGB before sending: DICOM Print Management
        cannot name a palette to a printer (PS3.3 Table C.13-5 allows only RGB
        in a Basic Color Image Sequence). --bit-depth and a lin-od presentation
        LUT therefore apply to grayscale film only.
  --annotate <annotate>   Text String (2030,0020) of a Basic Annotation Box
                          (repeatable; Annotation Position (2030,0010) is the
                          order given). Requires --annotation-format.
  --annotation-format <annotation-format>
                          Annotation Display Format ID (2010,0030), defined in
                          the printer's Conformance Statement (required with
                          --annotate)
  -r, --recursive         Recursively scan directories for DICOM files
  --dry-run               Show what would be printed without actually printing
  -v, --verbose           Show verbose output with progress
  --timeout <timeout>     Connection timeout in seconds (default: 60) (default:
                          60)
  --retries <retries>     Retry the print on connection/setup failure, up to N
                          times with exponential backoff (default: 0) (default:
                          0)
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

